       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That's double the labeled maximum of 3,200 mg/day for adults. The 1,600 mg single dose is also twice the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg. Doses at that level raise the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events.\n\nHere are some options within labeled limits:\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day). This is the maximum daily dose and is usually reserved for inflammatory conditions.\n- **400\u2013600 mg PO every 6 hours** for general pain or fever.\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day).\n\nDid you mean 600 mg or 800 mg, or 1600 mg as a total daily dose? Tell me the dose and frequency you want, plus the indication if you'd like it in the order note, and I'll enter it. If you need more analgesia than the maximum dose gives, adding acetaminophen or another agent might be better than raising the ibuprofen dose."
      }
